# Firstmate's test tier map: every tests/*.test.sh file has exactly one tier.
# bin/fm-test-run.sh owns what each tier means, when CI runs it, and the
# coverage check that keeps this map complete; docs/fm-test-portable-shards.md
# owns the rationale. Format: "<tier> <repo-relative test path>" per line, and
# `#` starts a comment. A new test file must be added here before CI passes.

